    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.08-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Conclusions, evaluation and justified improvements",
      "text": "A conclusion answers the enquiry question or hypothesis using the actual evidence. State whether the prediction is supported, partly supported or unsupported at the measured scale, then give relevant values and exceptions. A result need not support the hypothesis to be useful. The conclusion should not introduce new uncollected facts or extend one short sample into a claim about every season or an entire country.",
