    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.08-02",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A tourism hypothesis might predict greater path width at every rise in visitor count. Counts twenty,forty,sixty with widths 100,140,120 centimetres partly fit an initial rise but contradict the every-step prediction at the last site. Describe both parts. The result can show some association without showing a rise at every step or isolating visitor use as the sole cause of accumulated width.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-2",
