      "repair_note": "Claude cross-review repairs: 6137-4.1-001, 6137-4.1-002, 6137-4.1-003, 6137-4.1-004, 6137-4.1-005, 6137-4.2-005"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.08-03",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Score direction must be checked before judging environmental change. If zero means low pollution and five means high pollution, a rise from two to four indicates worse recorded pollution under that scale. It does not mean better water quality because the number is higher. A quality scale with the opposite direction could require the opposite interpretation. The label and key determine meaning.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-2",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-01-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-01-2",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-02-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-02-2",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-03-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-03-2"
      ],
      "context_tags": [
        "Geography",
        "original teaching"
      ],
      "assessment_objectives": [
        "A",
