    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.08-06",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Reliability concerns consistency under appropriate repeated conditions, while validity concerns whether the method addresses the intended concept or question. A count can be repeated consistently yet fail to measure residents' opinions. A questionnaire can ask relevant questions while its sample omits key groups. These dimensions explain why one improvement may strengthen a method without resolving every weakness.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-2",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-01-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-01-2",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-02-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-02-2",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-03-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-03-2"
      ],
      "context_tags": [
        "Geography",
        "original teaching"
      ],
      "assessment_objectives": [
        "A",
        "B",
        "C",
        "D"
      ],
      "claims_seen": {
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-1": 1,
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-2": 1,
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-01-1": 1,
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-01-2": 1,
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-02-1": 1,
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-02-2": 1,
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-03-1": 1,
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-03-2": 1
      },
      "authored_hash": "59d463c6c47a8ffee8d5d2c19924eac275a6c487beeb25e236959deeb4ca79bc"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.08-07",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A cause should not be claimed solely from association. A managed site with less litter after new bins might also have experienced a general clean-up or different weather. A suitable reference site, matched periods and context records can help test alternatives. They strengthen inference without removing every possible uncertainty. A precise conclusion can report improvement while keeping its exact attribution conditional.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-2",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-01-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-01-2",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-02-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-02-2",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-03-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-03-2"
      ],
      "context_tags": [
        "Geography",
        "original teaching"
      ],
      "assessment_objectives": [
        "A",
        "B",
        "C",
        "D"
      ],
      "claims_seen": {
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-1": 1,
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-2": 1,
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-01-1": 1,
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-01-2": 1,
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-02-1": 1,
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-02-2": 1,
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-03-1": 1,
