        "CL-6137-4.1.08-03-2": 1
      },
      "authored_hash": "adff1cd20b3059d3d94c14ede5c5d3586fffe66a61f7c8fd4ec4b8cb9b09140a"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.08-13",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A group survey can likewise have two judgements. Visitor positives of 80% exceed resident positives of 60%, supporting that comparison. A prediction that at least 75% of residents are positive is unsupported. The same data do not justify merging those statements into universal approval. Selection, sample size and time coverage remain relevant before extending the findings beyond the respondents.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-2",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-01-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.08-01-2",
