      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A justified improvement should specify the expected evidential gain. Clearer edge definitions improve comparability of widths; broader times improve temporal coverage; a suitable frame includes omitted groups; a relevant reference helps assess alternative explanations. These changes do different jobs. Naming one precisely is more useful than promising a perfect investigation with an undefined larger sample.",
